.TH VIELOTUS-SETTINGS 1 "November 2026" "VieLotusIM 2.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vielotus-settings \- configuration, macro/app rule manager, and diagnostics utility for Sen Viet (VieLotusIM)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vielotus-settings
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBvielotus-settings\fR opens the native GTK3 Bento Inspector for Sen Viet (VieLotusIM),
aligned with the macOS and Windows settings layout. The compact 640x420 main window provides
two tabs (\fBCài đặt\fR and \fBThông tin\fR) for input method selection (Telex or VNI),
free-tone SEN Flex composition, Quick Telex & Relaxed Coda abbreviations, Developer Mode
backtick code bypass, and inline live typing verification, plus modal sheets for the
Personal Macro Editor, Per-App Presentation Rules, Quick Feedback & Bug Reporter, and Linux-specific settings & diagnostics
(Preedit underline, GNOME per-window source state, Smart Bilingual, Modern Orthography, and
the IBus/Fcitx5/Wayland Environment Doctor).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-onboard\fR
One-shot first-install / first-login onboarding helper used by package installation and XDG Autostart to register Sen Viet automatically.
.TP
\fB\-\-telex\fR
Switch the active input method mode to Telex across IBus and Fcitx5.
.TP
\fB\-\-vni\fR
Switch the active input method mode to VNI across IBus and Fcitx5.
.TP
\fB\-\-activate\fR
Save and apply the current input method configuration to the active session without clobbering comments or custom keys.
.TP
\fB\-\-doctor\fR [\fB\-\-fix\fR]
Inspect Wayland/X11 session variables, running IBus/Fcitx5 daemons, dynamic library linkage (\fBldd \-r\fR),
and user configuration files. Pass \fB\-\-fix\fR to repair input source registration before reporting.
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR
Print the current 9 canonical configuration values to standard output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vielotus/config.env
User configuration file (preserved atomically with mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.config/vielotus/macros.json
Optional user macro dictionary overriding the factory defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.config/vielotus/typing-modes.yml
Optional per-application presentation rules (\fBpassthrough\fR, \fBdirectReplacement\fR, \fBmarkedText\fR, \fBautomatic\fR).
